@page "/terms"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>Terms and Conditions</PageTitle>

<div class="page-head">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Medical Manager</p>
        <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
        <p class="muted">Effective November 6, 2026. These terms cover use of Medical Manager and the text messages it sends.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<article class="legal-page">
    <p>
        Welcome to Medical Manager. By using Medical Manager, or by asking Medical Manager to send a text message, you agree to these terms.
        Medical Manager is a personal health record for blood pressure, blood sugar, lab results, medications, appointments, and to-dos.
        It is not a certified medical device and it does not replace a clinician.
        Product news and questions go through
        <a href="@SmsCopy.HomeUrl">www.medicalmgr.com</a>.
        Medical Manager is a service of @SmsCopy.BusinessName.
        Support email: <a href="mailto:@SmsCopy.SupportEmail">@SmsCopy.SupportEmail</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Text message program</h2>
    <p>
        <strong>Program name.</strong> Medical Manager.
        This program is live at <a href="@SmsCopy.HomeUrl">@SmsCopy.HomeUrl</a>.
        The public opt-in explanation is <a href="@SmsCopy.ConsentUrl">@SmsCopy.ConsentUrl</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        This number sends only one-time codes. Message types are a one-time approval code and a one-time monitor code. Appointment, medication, and to-do reminders are phone calls, not texts.
        Message frequency varies.
        Message and data rates may apply.
        Reply STOP to opt out.
        Reply HELP for help, or email <a href="mailto:@SmsCopy.SupportEmail">@SmsCopy.SupportEmail</a>.
        Read this page and the <a href="@SmsCopy.PrivacyUrl">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        The Profile consent box is unchecked until the patient checks it. Its label is:
        @SmsCopy.CheckboxLead
        <a href="privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Service description</h2>
    <p>
        Medical Manager stores the health records an account holder enters and shows them on that account's dashboard.
        A patient account can open only that patient's own records.
        A doctor account can open labs, blood pressure, or sugar only after the patient approves that request with a code sent to the patient's phone.
    </p>
    <p>
        Monitor Share sends a text when an account holder chooses to share the family monitor and presses Send.
        That text is only a one-time monitor code. It expires in 15 minutes and does not include a link or a name.
        The private link and the code are sent by email when an email address is entered.
        The person who receives the email opens the link and enters the code.
        The camera picture is shown only while the account holder leaves Monitor open.
        The text does not include blood pressure, blood sugar, lab results, medications, appointments, or a link.
    </p>
    <p>
        Appointment reminders are phone calls: one call the day before a visit, and one call an hour before, when appointment reminders are left on.
        Medication and to-do reminders are calls.
        Application reminders can also speak that same reminder on this device while you are signed in, with or without the phone reminders.
        These messages are informational. Medical Manager does not send marketing or promotional texts.
    </p>

    <h2>User responsibilities</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You agree to provide accurate information, including the mobile number you ask Medical Manager to text.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for keeping your account information secure, including your password and the Monitor Access Code.</li>
        <li>Share the family monitor only with a person who expects the link and passcode. You confirm that you have permission to text that mobile number.</li>
        <li>Treat the link and the four-digit passcode as private. Anyone who has both can see the camera picture while Monitor is open.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Messaging</h2>
    <p>
        <strong>Program name.</strong> Medical Manager.
    </p>
    <p>
        By checking the Profile text-message consent box, you consent to receive SMS messages from Medical Manager at the mobile number you enter.
        That box is unchecked until you check it. The same label is on the <a href="sms">text message consent</a> page.
        No approval text is sent unless that consent is saved for that number.
        Appointment reminders are calls and can be turned off on the profile page. They are not texts.
        Opt-in for a monitor code is separate: a signed-in account holder opens Monitor, chooses Share, enters a mobile number, and presses Send.
        No monitor text is sent unless that person presses Send.
    </p>
    <p>
        An approval text looks like this:
        "Medical Manager: Your one-time approval code is 123456. It expires in 15 minutes. Reply STOP to opt out. Reply HELP for help."
        A monitor text looks like this:
        "Medical Manager: Your one-time monitor code is 654321. It expires in 15 minutes. Reply STOP to opt out. Reply HELP for help."
        The digits in a real text are the code for that message. Neither text includes a link.
    </p>
    <p>
        Message frequency varies.
        A monitor text sends one one-time code each time an account holder presses Send for that mobile number.
        A chart-access text is sent to the mobile number already saved on the patient's profile when a doctor requests access to that patient's records.
        That text is a one-time approval code that expires in 15 minutes.
        The doctor does not see the code and does not choose the phone number.
        No chart-access text is sent unless the patient has saved a phone number and checked the text-message consent box.
    </p>
    <p>
        Message and data rates may apply.
        Contact your wireless carrier with questions about your text or data plan.
    </p>
    <p>
        You can opt out at any time by replying STOP to the number that sent the text.
        After you reply STOP, you will receive one confirmation, and then no further texts from that number.
        Reply START to allow texts again.
        Reply HELP for help, or email
        <a href="mailto:@SmsCopy.SupportEmail">@SmsCopy.SupportEmail</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
        Your information will be handled according to our <a href="privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
        No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.
        Text messaging originator opt-in data and consent will not be shared with any third parties.
        The phone number and the words of the text are sent to Twilio so the message can be delivered.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
        Medical Manager is a record-keeping and reminder tool. It does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.
        We are not liable for any damages resulting from the use of our services, including a missed reminder, a delayed text, or use of a family monitor link by someone who received the link and passcode.
        Wireless carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to terms</h2>
    <p>
        We may update these terms at any time.
        When these terms change, the effective date at the top of this page changes with them.
        Continued use of our services means you accept the changes.
        This page is public. You can read it before you create an account.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
        For questions, contact us through <a href="https://www.medicalmgr.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">medicalmgr.com</a>.
        Reply HELP to a Medical Manager text for help with messages.
        Read the <a href="privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and the <a href="hipaa">HIPAA compliance confirmation</a> for how health information is handled.
    </p>
</article>
